 nginx,
 ca-certificates
Recommends: postgresql (>= 15)
Description: ATProto book catalogue appview and labeler
 A SvelteKit appview for the community.lexicon.book lexicons, backed by
 PostgreSQL. It indexes records from the ATProto firehose via TAP, serves
 XRPC queries, hosts the web catalogue, and issues its own labels so other
 appviews can consume its curation decisions by DID.
 .
 This package installs the prebuilt server payload at /usr/lib/bibliograph and
 runs it under systemd as the unprivileged "bibliograph" user: a web unit, a
 worker unit consuming TAP, and a oneshot migrator both require. Configuration
 lives in /etc/bibliograph/bibliograph.env.
 .
 The Node.js runtime is deliberately not bundled. Install it from the
 NodeSource apt repository (https://deb.nodesource.com/node_22.x/ or newer),
 which satisfies this package's versioned dependency with whatever newer
 release it publishes. The distro's own nodejs (18.x on Debian 12 and Ubuntu
 24.04) does not.
 .
 PostgreSQL is only a Recommends: the database may be remote. Set DATABASE_URL
 in the configuration file either way.
